@sde1000 there is no such config option in the official documentation: https://docs.joinmastodon.org/admin/config/ 
However, from the server I am able to access ipv4 only server (GitHub is a very good test for that ) 

My sidekiq shows me > 2.900 completed and > 1700 failed

@ClearlyClaire may have a different opinion, but I think it is.

Although I brought up the issue in the context of an IPv6-only system connecting to systems with both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, it's equally applicable to IPv4-only systems connecting to systems with both types of address.

For example, prior to the patch an IPv4-only system needing to connect to another system with two IPv4 and two IPv6 addresses may find that after the `.take(2)` it ends up with two IPv6 addresses that it can't use. After the patch, this problem goes away.

but finally my problem was the missing webfinger config in nginx. I added:

`location /.well-known/webfinger {
  return 301 https://mastodon.example.com$request_uri;
}`

and now I receive all the messages I was missing
